  "description": "Revocations of the b01-bind-v3 device read from their signed statements alone (SPEC §3.5). revocation_bare and revocation_misfiled carry the r01 revocation statement and binding_sig under odd tags: the first has only d and binding_sig, the second is filed under another address and names another device_id and a live-looking device_pk. Both retire the b01 bind and leave the r01 re-bind, signed later, live. revocation_undated is signed by the address but signs no revoked_at: it retires every bind of the device, the later re-bind too. The address and key are BIP-322’s own published test vector key (P2WPKH, mainnet); never use them for anything real.",
